# Backend Core Standards

- Use `@/` alias imports for code from `src`; do not introduce new deep relative paths like `../../../`.
- For runtime validation, use Zod from `@/lib/zod` and schemas from `src/schemas`.
- For API errors, use `throwAPIError(...)` instead of ad-hoc local error formats.
- Return route responses through `responseSchema.parse(...)` before `c.json(...)`.
- For new public APIs, keep OpenAPI metadata meaningful (`title`, `description`, `ref`).
- Avoid `any`; if strict typing is not possible yet, use `unknown` with narrowing.
- Do not mix policy and workflow: coding standards belong to rules, step-by-step procedures belong to skills.

## Required Self-Check Before Finishing

- Changes remain type-safe and do not introduce unjustified linter suppressions.
- Added/updated API handlers follow existing schema/response patterns.
- If environment integration was changed, all config propagation points are verified.
